HST Office: "Dùng HST Office để mở tài liệu văn phòng" on the Typical setup path.

A checkbox on the setup-type page, shown only for Typical (the Custom path keeps its per-type
file-type page). Ticked (HSTDEFAULTAPPS=1):
- SELECT_WORD, SELECT_EXCEL and SELECT_POWERPOINT are set before Regallmsdocdll, so the Office
  file types are registered to HST Office even where another program had them; the
  Capabilities entries are registered as before;
- the DWORD ChosenAtInstall = 1 is written under Software\HASON TECH\HST Office\DefaultApps
  (HKLM for a per-machine install, HKCU per user), which the first start reads so that it
  does not ask again. Unticked, the value is absent.

Windows keeps each user's own choice of default app (UserChoice), which no installer may set;
the first-start prompt then opens Settings at HST Office. The checkbox text promises no more.

Whether the box starts ticked is one switch, HSTDEFAULTAPPSUI in Property.idt (0 = unticked, the
current default; 1 = ticked). HSTDEFAULTAPPS itself stays unset by default, because a checkbox
shows ticked whenever its property has any value; when the switch is 1, HstDefaultAppsOn (UI
sequence only) sets it. Silent installs and the updater change nothing unless HSTDEFAULTAPPS=1
is passed on the command line. Choosing Custom clears it (its NewDialog event moves after the
clearing event).

